<title>AUSTRALIA: C-C Amatil up 4 pct to new 97 high on deal.</title>
<headline>C-C Amatil up 4 pct to new 97 high on deal.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Australian-based soft drink bottler Coca-Cola Amatil Ltd jumped 61 cents or almost four percent to a new 1997 high of A$16.01 in active Wednesday morning trade after it removed any lingering uncertainty over its deal with San Miguel Corp.</p>
<p>C-C Amatil announced that it had signed the deal with San Miguel to buy its Philippine Coca-Cola bottling assets in exchange for 25 percent of C-C Amatil shares.</p>
<p>C-C Amatil agreed to San Miguel requests for an extra board member, allaying concerns by some Philippine shareholders about a lack of San Miguel representation on the CCA board.</p>
</text>
